Contains a SECOND, unrelated change swept in from a concurrent session:
A1.4 deferred tool loading (fsr_playbooks/llm/anthropic_provider.py,
run_turn.py, tests/test_provider_capability_matrix.py). Its intended message:

  llm: deferred tool loading for the long tail (A1.4)

  Anthropic tool search + defer_loading on the materialized MCP tools, BM25
  search tool prepended. Schemas are APPENDED on search, never swapped, so a
  dynamic surface and a warm cache stop being mutually exclusive.

  The split is mcp_*, NOT the page's ranked head: deferring by page would put
  the array back to varying mid-session, the exact cache defect A1.3 removed.

  Both API constraints enforced here rather than at the wire -- the search tool
  is never itself deferred, and an all-deferrable slice is left alone instead
  of earning 400 'All tools have defer_loading set'.

  Opt-in via run_agent_turn(defer_tools=True); a caller that does not ask gets
  a byte-identical array, asserted.

  P2 unchanged -- DISCOVERY only. Tier-3, the affordance gates, per-config
  scoping and persona scopes all still decide execution.
